* The display and simulation-control tasks in a transient run (2.8.0).
* A 1 V step charges C1 through R1 (RC = 1 ms); models/tasks/rc_watch.va watches `out`.
* Expected, from V(out) = 1 - exp(-t/RC):
*   - one $strobe line when V(out) rises through 0.9 V, at t = RC*ln(10) = 2.3026e-3 s
*     (to the step control's resolution: the crossing is interpolated between accepted points);
*   - one $display line and the run ending at the first accepted point past 0.95 V,
*     t >= RC*ln(20) = 2.9957e-3 s, well before the deck's 10 ms stop time;
*   - va-cli's note that $finish ended the analysis there.
* Run: va-cli sim circuits/tasks/rc_watch.net --model models/tasks --tran --report out
V1 in gnd 1.0
R1 in out 1000
C1 out gnd 1e-6
X1 out rc_watch
.tran 20u 10m UIC
.end
